      "writtenOn": "2026-05-12T17:29:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Some initial comments inline.\n\nA couple of high-level concerns:\n\n1) No \"true\" incremental decoding: while we do satisfy the interface, it looks like we\u0027re re-decoding the whole image on every iteration.  Hopefully this is something that can be addressed upstream?\n\n2) No scanline decoding support: we\u0027re forced to buffer the whole image, which increases memory pressure.  Is this something that could be retrofitted to Zune?",
      "revId": "2cec39b4405ecb9a90e54f654cd84b4512da286a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4d37b2ae_70dab5b0",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 4159917
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-14T10:08:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good points. In both cases we will require changes in zune-jpeg (which are already in progress). My idea is to complete that in a follow up CL in which we update required patches to zune-jpeg and then make use of new APIs to support incremental decoding and scanline consumption of decoded image.",
      "parentUuid": "6bde025f_e4770ba9",
      "revId": "2cec39b4405ecb9a90e54f654cd84b4512da286a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
